/E (The collaboration profile indicates that SPPU's research output is strongly anchored by domestic publishing, driven primarily by extensive national and institutional partnerships. However, the university records a more moderate international collaboration percentage of 17.8% compared to several other Maharashtra State public universities visible in the dataset. Going forward, strategically expanding international collaborative research networks may support greater global research visibility, drive higher citation performance, and enhance high-impact research output. From a research assessment perspective, scaling international co-authorship remains a critical component of strengthening the university's global research footprint and overall competitiveness.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [8]
